@page "/page-e"

@* NON-streaming static SSR: the whole render is one synchronous walk that starts only once
   the awaits below have completed. It then swaps BOTH of HeadOutlet's outlets late — the
   title section via PageTitle and the head-content section via HeadContent (the public
   SectionContent for HeadOutlet's second SectionOutlet). Two outlets, two content renderers,
   both replaced from a continuation. *@
@if (_ready)
{
    <PageTitle>Page E</PageTitle>
    <HeadContent>
        <meta name="repro-page" content="page-e" />
    </HeadContent>
}

<h1>Page E</h1>
<p>Static SSR, both head outlets swapped after an await.</p>

@code {
    private bool _ready;

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        await Task.Delay(Random.Shared.Next(1, 6));
        _ready = true;
    }
}
